{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.Mu4RhoFCluster","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu4RhoFCluster","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.mu4_sign_consistent_with_pairwise_cluster","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.mu4_sign_consistent_with_pairwise_cluster","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu4RhoFCluster.lean#L126-L135","doc":"**(Sign-consistency, not a derivation.)**  The 4-body residual coefficient is\n*negative* (`μ₄ = −4.591 < 0`) and the pairwise-product 4-body cluster content\nis also `≤ 0` (a special case of `one_sub_prod_le_oneSum`), so the two lie in\nthe same non-positive half-line — the signs are consistent.  This is recorded\nhonestly as *consistency*, NOT a magnitude derivation: `μ₄` is dominated by the\nderived graded reference's own 4-body simplex coefficient `g₄ = +8.37` being\nsubtracted (`μ₄ = s₄ − g₄`), not by the `ρ_F` cluster. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.mu3_ne_pairwise_3body_cluster","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.mu3_ne_pairwise_3body_cluster","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu4RhoFCluster.lean#L109-L122","doc":"**(WALL) μ₃ is unreachable by any pairwise ρ_F cluster.**  The residual 3-body\nsimplex coefficient `μ₃` is *positive* (`+0.4708`), but the beyond-pairwise\n3-body content of any pairwise interface product `∏ fᵢ`, `fᵢ ∈ [0,1]`, is\n`≤ 0`.  Hence `μ₃ ≠` that cluster content — the multiplicative ρ_F cluster\nroute cannot supply `μ₃`.  (The only pairwise escape `fᵢ > 1` is foreclosed at\n`q₀ ≈ 1.110` by `markovZD_lt_one_iff`: `z = q³/(q²+1) < 1` iff `q³ < q² + 1`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.pairwise_3body_content_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.pairwise_3body_content_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu4RhoFCluster.lean#L95-L107","doc":"**Pairwise 3-body content is non-positive** (the `productModel_3body_nonpos`\ncontent with `c = 1`).  For `f_a,f_b,f_c ∈ [0,1]`,\n`f_a + f_b + f_c − f_a f_b f_c − 2 ≤ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.one_sub_prod_le_oneSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.one_sub_prod_le_oneSum","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu4RhoFCluster.lean#L74-L91","doc":"**Beyond-pairwise content of a pairwise product is non-positive** (Weierstrass\nunion bound).  For `fᵢ ∈ [0,1]`, `1 − ∏ fᵢ ≤ Σ (1 − fᵢ)`; equivalently the\nbeyond-pairwise cluster content `(1 − ∏ fᵢ) − Σ(1 − fᵢ) ≤ 0`.  This is the\ngeneral (any bond-count) form covering both the 3-body and 4-body clusters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.oneSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.oneSum","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu4RhoFCluster.lean#L71-L72","doc":"`oneSum l = Σ (1 − fᵢ)`, the pairwise (1-bond) content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.prod_mem_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.prod_mem_unit","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu4RhoFCluster.lean#L56-L69","doc":"All factors in `[0,1]` ⇒ the product lies in `[0,1]`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}